## 🚀 Feature Proposal

In some cases, it might be useful for our users to know if they are inside a 404 handling or not. We can quickly check it internally via the `kFourOhFourContext` symbol, but I think it would be great to expose it in our public API via the request object.

## Motivation

A use case example can be found [here](https://twitter.com/ThisIsMissEm/status/1240644657970806791).
TL;DR, you may not want to parse the body in case of a 404 request and close the request as soon as possible.

## Example

```js
fastify.addHook('onRequest', (req, reply, done) => {
  if (req.is404) {
    // specific handling
  }
  done()
})
```

The `is404` should always be present in the request object defaulting to `false`, and should be set to `true` automatically by Fastify.

